(* Transport variant (b), authenticated: a party accepts a message as coming
   from endpoint `src` only if that endpoint's key authenticated it for this
   destination. The attacker has endpoints of its own and can authenticate
   as those, but not as an honest endpoint.

   This is weaker than a real mutually authenticated channel: it gives no
   confidentiality, and a message authenticated once can be replayed to the
   same destination on any later connection. Whatever holds here holds over
   a real authenticated channel. *)
reduc forall k: esk, dst: ep, m: bitstring;
  transportAccepts(epk(k), dst, m, tsig(k, dst, m)) = true.
